  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "An equilateral triangle has side length $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine the triangle’s inradius.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}}$.\n\nFind the altitude, then use $A=\\frac{1}{2}Pr$.",
          "worked": "The altitude bisects the base. By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=a^2-\\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2\\\\h^2&=\\frac{3a^2}{4}\\\\h&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing $P=3a$ and $A=\\frac{1}{2}Pr$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2}(3a)r&=\\frac{1}{2}ah\\\\r&=\\frac{h}{3}\\\\r&=\\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Determine the triangle’s circumradius.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}$.\n\nThe common centre lies on an altitude, so $R=h-r$.",
          "worked": "In an equilateral triangle, each altitude is both an angle bisector and a perpendicular bisector of the opposite side. Thus the incentre and circumcentre coincide. On an altitude, the distance from this centre to the base is $r$, and its distance to the opposite vertex is $R$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}R&=h-r\\\\R&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}-\\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\\\R&=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
